  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a July 2025 statement, Allende described Florida department efforts to build an AI use policy and address privacy and responsible-use risks. Later DHS statements attributed to him describe investing in next-generation tools and prize challenges to recognize biological risks and support biosurveillance. He also said that security and prosperity depend on understanding and controlling technologies underpinning critical infrastructure and the bioeconomy, and that launching challenges is decisive action for resilience and innovation. A reported statement notes that detection algorithms are key to reducing false alarms and checkpoint wait times.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s5",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s6"
   ],
